msgid "yes — the identity provider is the invitation"
msgstr "bai: identitate-hornitzailea da gonbidapena"

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: a person may have a picture of the whole page kept, sent by their browser extension or drawn here from the kept source with scripts and the network off. A picture taken in somebody's browser shows the page as they were seeing it, signed in or not. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep one."
msgstr "Bai: pertsona batek orri osoaren irudi bat gorde dezake, bere nabigatzaile-hedapenak bidalia edo hemen gordetako iturburutik marraztua, scriptak eta sarea itzalita. Norbaiten nabigatzailean ateratako irudi batek orria haiek ikusten zuten bezala erakusten du, saioa hasita edo ez. Ez, edo ezarri gabe: inoren kapturek ez dute halakorik gordetzen."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: a person may have the page's source kept beside what was read from it, exactly as it was parsed, so that a capture can be checked against it and read again by a better parser. It is kept as text and never shown as a page. No, or not set: nobody's captures keep it, whatever they have chosen."
msgstr "Bai: pertsona batek orriaren iturburua gorde dezake handik irakurritakoaren ondoan, analizatu zen bezalaxe, kaptura harekin egiaztatu eta analizatzaile hobe batek berriro irakur dezan. Testu gisa gordetzen da, eta ez da inoiz orri gisa erakusten. Ez, edo ezarri gabe: inoren kapturek ez dute gordetzen, edozer aukeratu dutela ere."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: anyone who finds the address may create an account. No: invitation only. An empty instance always offers the sign-up form, so somebody can become the first account."
msgstr "Bai: helbidea aurkitzen duen edonork sor dezake kontu bat. Ez: gonbidapenez soilik. Instantzia huts batek beti eskaintzen du izen-emateko inprimakia, norbait lehen kontua izan dadin."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: somebody who arrives through the identity provider is signed straight in, without being asked for a code as well. Say yes only if you know that provider checks identity at least as carefully as Postulo would. It never applies to a password sign-in, and it removes nobody's authenticator app. A passkey already counts on its own and needs no setting."
msgstr "Bai: identitate-hornitzailearen bidez datorrenak zuzenean hasten du saioa, kode bat ere eskatu gabe. Erantzun baietz soilik hornitzaile horrek identitatea gutxienez Postulok bezain arretaz egiaztatzen duela badakizu. Ez da inoiz aplikatzen pasahitzarekin saioa hastean, eta ez dio inori autentifikazio-aplikazioa kentzen. Sarbide-gakoak berez balio du, eta ez du ezarpenik behar."

#: src/postulo/core/server_forms.py
msgid "Yes: somebody who has forgotten their password can ask for a code at their primary address and type it back. A code rather than a link, because mail scanners follow links and would spend one before the person read it. It is never a second factor: an authenticator app is still asked for. Offered only while this instance's mail is actually getting through."
msgstr "Bai: pasahitza ahaztu duenak kode bat eska dezake bere helbide nagusira, eta gero idatzi. Kodea, eta ez esteka, posta-eskanerrek estekak irekitzen dituztelako eta pertsonak mezua irakurri aurretik erabiliko luketelako. Ez da inoiz bigarren faktorea: autentifikazio-aplikazioa eskatzen da oraindik. Instantzia honen posta benetan iristen den bitartean soilik eskaintzen da."

